/// Every token of the baseline theme, by group: written by scripts/docsite/reference.py from `wf theme --json`;
/// edit the compiler or the script, not this file.

page TokensPage(path: "/reference/tokens", title: "Design tokens — Reference", description: "Every baseline design token with its default value, how a theme overrides one, and how a style block or a stylesheet reads it, by full or short name.") {
    ReferenceItemShell(t("tokens.title"), summary: t("tokens.lede", { count: 71 }), signature: "theme Brand \{ color-primary: #3B82F6 \}", group: t("tokens.title"), entries: REFERENCE_PAGES, sections: [Anchor(id: "tokens-color", label: "color"), Anchor(id: "tokens-spacing", label: "spacing"), Anchor(id: "tokens-font-size", label: "font-size"), Anchor(id: "tokens-line-height", label: "line-height"), Anchor(id: "tokens-radius", label: "radius"), Anchor(id: "tokens-shadow", label: "shadow"), Anchor(id: "tokens-transition", label: "transition"), Anchor(id: "tokens-font", label: "font"), Anchor(id: "tokens-motion", label: "motion"), Anchor(id: "tokens-other", label: "other"), Anchor(id: "reading-a-token", label: "Reading a token"), Anchor(id: "the-baseline", label: "The baseline"), Anchor(id: "short-names", label: "Short names")], source: "md-docs/reference/design-tokens.md") {
        notes {
            Stack(gap: .lg) {
                Markdown("This chapter lists every design token of the baseline theme with its value, and how a style reads one. A *design token* is a named value — a colour, a size, a duration — that every built-in is drawn with. Change a token and every element drawn with it changes.\n\nA `theme` declaration changes the tokens it names and keeps the baseline value of every other one. A theme may also add tokens of its own. Each token becomes a CSS custom property on `:root`:")

                CodeBlock(#"theme Brand {
    color-primary: #0F766E
    radius-md: 14px
    screen-md: 900px
    surface-raised: #F1F5F9
}"#, title: "wf")

                Markdown("The build writes to `:root` only the tokens something in the output names, and the tokens those name in turn.")

                Heading("Reading a token", id: "reading-a-token").h2

                Markdown("A token has two spellings, one for each place a style is written:")

                Table(caption: "Reading a token") {
                    Table.Head {
                        Table.Row {
                            Table.Cell("Where").header
                            Table.Cell("Syntax").header
                            Table.Cell("Example").header
                        }
                    }
                    Table.Body {
                        Table.Row {
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("A `style \{ \}` block") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`$name`") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`background: $color-surface`") }
                        }
                        Table.Row {
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("A `style \{ \}` block, short form") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`$suffix`, resolved by the property's group ([below](#short-names))") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`padding: $lg` is `spacing-lg`") }
                        }
                        Table.Row {
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("A `.css` file under `src/`") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`var(--name)`") }
                            Table.Cell { Markdown("`color: var(--color-text-muted)`") }
                        }
                    }
                }

                Markdown("This page reads the tokens of the theme above — one the theme adds, one it changes, one it keeps, and a breakpoint it moves:")

                CodeBlock(#"theme Brand {
    color-primary: #0F766E
    radius-md: 14px
    screen-md: 900px
    surface-raised: #F1F5F9
}

page Pricing(path: "/pricing", title: "Pricing", description: "Plans and prices for every team.") {
    Heading("Pricing").h1
    Card {
        style {
            background: $surface-raised
            padding: $lg
            border-radius: $md
            border: 1px solid $border
            @md { padding: $xl }
        }
        Text("Team plan").bold
    }
}"#, title: "wf")

                Markdown("The card's background is `#F1F5F9`, its radius `14px` and its border the baseline `color-border`. Its padding grows to `spacing-xl` from `900px` wide, because `@md` reads `screen-md`.\n\nA `$token` the resolved theme does not declare draws the `V06` warning, since the property would fall back to nothing. `wf theme` lists every token the build uses, where each is read, and the contrast of the colour pairs ([Command line](/reference/cli#wf-theme)).")

                Heading("The baseline", id: "the-baseline").h2

                Markdown("The tables below are written from the compiler's baseline theme, and the test suite checks them against it.")

                Heading("Colour", id: "colour").h3

                Table(caption: "Colour") {
                    Table.Head {
                        Table.Row {
                            Table.Cell("Token").header
                            Table.Cell("Baseline").header
                        }
                    }
